x11: fix integrated title bar drag cancelled by stale/early mouse events

Integrated title bar drag on X11 fails when:
- button pressed while the mouse is moving;
- bar pressed again right after a drag/click without moving.

Cause: request_drag_move() sets `dragging` and sends _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE.
The WM then owns the pointer and consumes the release, so any mouse
event we get while `dragging` runs cancel_drag(): send MOVERESIZE_CANCEL,
synthesize Left release, and drop the event.
- Motion queued after the press (request is spawned async) or arriving
  before the WM grabs -> CANCEL sent right after the request, drag aborted.
- `dragging` stays set after a completed drag -> next ButtonPress is
  swallowed and no drag is requested.

Fix:
- Ignore MotionNotify while `dragging` and Button1 is held (pre-grab
  motion). Release or button-up motion still ends the drag.
- After clearing a stale drag, still dispatch the event; drop only a
  real release (cancel_drag already synthesized one).

Tested on muffin (Cinnamon).

